x86_64-linux  Three names cxx1 emits and clang does not, all definitions nothing here calls: `_ZN2VBC1Ev` and `_ZN2VBD1Ev`, VB's complete-object forms where VB is only ever a base, and `_ZN2VEC2Ev`, VE's base-subobject constructor where nothing derives from VE. Every name this case is about agrees - the virtual thunks `_ZTv0_n24_N2VD1fEv` and `_ZTv0_n32_N2VDD1Ev`/`D0Ev`, `_ZTT2VD`, `_ZTT2VE`, `_ZTC2VE0_2VD` - and the tables' words are compared against clang's in the header of the .cpp.
arm64-darwin  The same, less `__ZN2VBD1Ev`, which this target's clang emits too; Mach-O's leading underscore on the rest.
